  },
  "2805": {
    "document_id": "2805",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "The text is a statement by Senator Feinstein criticizing the EPA's ruling on mercury emissions. This is an example of position-taking (expressing opposition to a policy) without claiming any personal or collective responsibility for a tangible outcome. According to the negative clarification, this does not qualify as credit-claiming."
