    "document_id": "3728",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "The text describes a bipartisan group of senators, including Senator Conrad, demanding a vote on a bill for farm disaster aid. However, the bill has not yet passed or secured any tangible benefits. According to the negative clarification, merely introducing or advocating for a bill without indicating its passage or securing concrete outcomes does not qualify as credit-claiming."
  },
  "3880": {
    "document_id": "3880",
